{"kind":"assert","text":"H2 byte admission (232cbf9d): approved, with these bounds.\n1. Scope. H2 admits canonical prepare and commit entries in packages/bytes/src/records.ts through the shared parser and keeper, so that isEntry and isEntryOf reach the verified-source judgment. The other sequenced tags stay refused, as do the Scope pin guard and the H4 runtime. Bound each new field by the existing record limits; GroupReadUse arrays at most four, as the act mark allows.\n2. Placement. The entry's top level is canonical, as the SequenceEntry comment and sequenced note sections 5.2 and 5.5 say: a prepare entry states position and reads, a commit entry states position, and no other entry states either. H1 also put position and reads in the prepare input. H2 keeps that contract and adds no wire change: entryOf copies both from the prepare input to the top level, entryOf gives a commit its prepare's position, and the validator refuses a prepare entry whose top-level fields differ from its input's, and any other entry that states them.\n3. Open point for H4, recorded in the H2 note amendment: the duplicate copy in the prepare input. Removing it changes entry hashes, so the decision comes before any live sequenced entry exists. Name it; do not decide it in H2.\nWitness: one admitted prepare and one admitted commit from real entryOf output reach the source judgment; a prepare with mismatched top-level position, and an ordinary act entry that states reads, are refused.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}